## FFUF — Fast web discovery

Find folders and files:

```bash
ffuf -u http://TARGET/FUZZ -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt -fc 404
```

- `FUZZ` is where FFUF inserts words.
- `-fc 404` hides normal “not found” pages.

Check common extensions:

```bash
ffuf -u http://TARGET/FUZZ -w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt -e .php,.html,.txt -fc 404
```

Look for virtual hosts in an authorised lab:

```bash
ffuf -u http://TARGET -H "Host: FUZZ.target.local" -w /usr/share/seclists/Discovery/DNS/subdomains-top1million-5000.txt -fs 0
```

---

## Feroxbuster — Website content discovery

```bash
feroxbuster -u http://TARGET
```

Specify extensions:

```bash
feroxbuster -u http://TARGET -x php,html,txt
```

Save findings:

```bash
feroxbuster -u http://TARGET -o feroxbuster.txt
```

Use either Feroxbuster, Gobuster, or FFUF at first. You do not need all three every time.

---

## Nikto — Basic web-server checks

```bash
nikto -h http://TARGET
```

Nikto looks for common exposed files, server misconfigurations, and known web-server issues. It can be noisy, so use it only against an authorised lab.

